+ * Soundness rests on who can change a TLB entry while a TB runs: only the
+ * vCPU thread (cross-thread flushes are queued with async_run_on_cpu and
+ * run between TBs), and only inside a helper -- a call op, or a memop's
+ * own slow path.  Both kill every memo on the way back, so a memo is
+ * valid wherever control reaches it, whatever path it took; labels and
+ * the guest-loop back-edge need no work.  The kinds stay separate because
+ * addr_read and addr_write are separate permissions (a clean-for-reads
+ * page can still be write-protected for SMC).  A fresh wasm local reads 0,
